<title>USA: Pratt says wins FAA engine approval.</title>
<headline>Pratt says wins FAA engine approval.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Technologies Corp. unit Pratt &amp; Whitney said Wednesday it had received certification by the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) for the PW4090, the most powerful jet engine it has ever built.</p>
<p>The first Pratt-powered Boeing 777-200 increased gross weight aircraft will be delivered to UAL Corp's United Airlines in early March, Pratt said in a statement.</p>
<p>The engine is rated at 90,000 pounds of take-off thrust, and follows the PW4084 which launched 777 service in June 1995.</p>
<p>Pratt also said it is the first company to have begun ground testing of a 98,000-pound thrust engine.</p>
<p>--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224</p>
